Amazon OpenSearch Serverless supports endpoint policies for VPCs. An endpoint policy is an
IAM resource-based policy that you attach to a VPC endpoint to control which AWS principals can
use the endpoint to access your AWS service. For more information, see Control access to VPC
endpoints using endpoint policies.
To use an endpoint policy, you must ﬁrst create an interface endpoint. You can create an interface
endpoint using either the OpenSearch Serverless console or the OpenSearch Serverless API. After
