you create your interface endpoint, you will need to add the endpoint policy to the endpoint. For
more information, see Access Amazon OpenSearch Serverless using an interface endpoint (AWS
PrivateLink).
Note
You can't deﬁne an endpoint policy directly in the OpenSearch Service console.
An endpoint policy does not override or replace other identity-based policies, resource-based
policies, network policies, or data access policies you may have conﬁgured. For more information
on updating endpoint policies, see Control access to VPC endpoints using endpoint policies.
By default, an endpoint policy grants full access to your VPC endpoint.
{
"Statement": [
{
"Effect": "Allow",
"Principal": "*",
"Action": "*",
"Resource": "*"
}
]
}
Although the default VPC endpoint policy grants full endpoint access, you can conﬁgure a VPC
endpoint policy to allow access to speciﬁc roles and users. To do this, see the following example:
JSON
{
"Version":"2012-10-17",
"Statement": [
{
"Effect": "Allow",
"Principal": {
"AWS": [
"123456789012",
"987654321098"
